    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "klwumqo",
      "content": "The Constitution of India devotes Part XVII (Articles 343 to 351) entirely to the subject of Official Language. This is the legal and constitutional foundation on which the entire Rajbhasha policy of India is built. The Constituent Assembly debated this extensively before arriving at these provisions."
    },
    {
      "id": "a8aenkt",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Article</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Subject Matter</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Provision</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 343(1)</p>",
            "<p>Official Language of the Union</p>",
            "<p>Hindi in Devanagari script shall be the official language of the Union; numerals in international form of Indian numerals (0-9)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 343(2)</p>",
            "<p>Continuation of English</p>",
            "<p>English to continue for 15 years after Constitution commencement (i.e., till 26 January 1965) for official purposes; Parliament may extend</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 343(3)</p>",
            "<p>Parliament's power</p>",
            "<p>Parliament may by law provide for continued use of English after 15 years; this led to Official Languages Act, 1963</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 344</p>",
            "<p>Commission and Parliamentary Committee</p>",
            "<p>President to constitute Rajbhasha Commission 5 years after commencement and then every 10 years; Parliamentary Committee to examine commission's report</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 345</p>",
            "<p>Official Language(s) of a State</p>",
            "<p>Legislature of a State may adopt Hindi or any of the languages in use in that state as official language</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 346</p>",
            "<p>Official Language for Union-State Communications</p>",
            "<p>English to be used for official communication between Union and State until Parliament provides otherwise; two non-Hindi states may agree to use Hindi</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 347</p>",
            "<p>Special Provision for Languages</p>",
            "<p>President may recognise language used by substantial section of population of any state</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 348</p>",
            "<p>Language in Supreme Court, HCs, and Parliament</p>",
            "<p>Proceedings of SC and HCs, bills, acts, ordinances, etc. :English; till Parliament provides otherwise</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 348(2)</p>",
            "<p>HC proceedings in Hindi/State Language</p>",
            "<p>Governor may with President's consent authorise use of Hindi or state official language in HC proceedings (except judgments/orders/decrees)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 349</p>",
            "<p>Special procedure for language bills</p>",
            "<p>Bill to provide for language to be used for any official purpose :President's prior sanction required; must consult Rajbhasha Commission</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 350</p>",
            "<p>Language for representations</p>",
            "<p>Every person has right to submit a representation for redress of grievance in any language used in the Union or in the State</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 350A</p>",
            "<p>Primary education in mother tongue</p>",
            "<p>Every State shall provide adequate facility for instruction in mother tongue at primary level to children of linguistic minorities</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 350B</p>",
            "<p>Special Officer for Linguistic Minorities</p>",
            "<p>President shall appoint a Special Officer (Commissioner for Linguistic Minorities) to investigate matters relating to safeguards for linguistic minorities</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 351</p>",
            "<p>Directive for Development of Hindi</p>",
            "<p>It shall be the duty of the Union to promote the spread of Hindi; develop it so it serves as medium of expression for composite culture of India; draws primarily on Sanskrit and secondarily on other languages</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
